{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head 3be00804e501e4f30e8cf653b6dd1ce8de72a25e, resting on all 66 artifacts with packages/client/README.md first.\n\nValidation: clean installation, repository strict type checks, 79 client Node tests plus 2 workerd tests, 32 CLI tests, and 66 MCP Node tests plus 1 workerd test passed independently. CLI build, bundled --help and dry-run package inspection passed. Four independent diagnostic tests reproduce the three remaining findings below; an additional positive MCP test confirms a valid bearer recovers its original proposal after its lease ends. Test files: /tmp/artroom-checker-clients-v2/packages/{client,cli,mcp}/test/checker-v2-review.test.ts. These are local tests against the submitted fake Room and native Web Streams, not deployed acceptance tests. Production sources were not changed. Reviewed changed source, tests, documentation and lock descriptors; identical artifacts retain the previous review's inspection. CLI tests report one obsolete snapshot, without a failing assertion.\n\nReview f47a509c: first-request bearer redaction, watch session replacement and observable termination, login/redemption completion journals, prepared-act replay after changed HEAD/lease, operation-following wait, and own-property MCP boundaries repair their demonstrated cases. The new RPC bearer adapter, because propagation, same-read AttentionPage and structured explain-not-found result follow amendment 2. Keep these tests. Prepared replay and the journal are useful additions, but the restart behavior remains incomplete below.\n\n1. [P2, Architecture/receipt recovery] Do not gate a retained signed act's replay on creating a fresh read session. Every act command calls open at packages/cli/src/main.ts:183-194 before journaled examines its saved envelope. connect reads genesis through a new signed session request. After the signing key is retired, that request is refused even though R-IDEM-2 and amendment 2 require the retained signed envelope to return its original receipt. The independent test drops all four claim responses, retains its journal, retires the signing key and ends read sessions. Direct RoomWire.submit of the exact saved signature returns the original claim sequence; the next CLI run fails unauthenticated before making any /acts request and leaves the journal unfinished. A saved signed act needs a direct, room-bound replay path that does not require new signing/read authority or current lane facts. Keep normal connection verification for new work, the room-ID check on retained envelopes, and the auth-first rule for unsigned bearer retries. Test restart with a retired/revoked key, a failed genesis/session read, and a previously recorded refusal. The existing amendment test replays on the same already-connected handle and therefore misses this boundary.\n\n2. [P2, Architecture/local completion] Keep an act journal until its local completion steps are durable. journaled deletes its entry and clears ctx.act at main.ts:277-278 as soon as it receives a remote result. Claim, land and release perform local config/credential work afterward. The independent landing test makes the config write at lines 539-541 fail after land is admitted: the operation is live, the saved envelope is gone, config has no landing, the error offers no journal retry key, and artroom wait has nothing to follow. After the lease ends, repeating the explicit original idempotency key rebuilds from current state and refuses not-holder instead of recovering that operation. Retain the prepared envelope and, where needed, its result until operation/config/credential changes finish; remove the journal only after completion. An interruption after remote success must resume the same result and local steps without preflight or another land. Add interruptions at remote-result receipt, before and after config writes, and during release credential removal, including failed disk writes. The README's 'every local step is done' promise currently holds for login/redeem, not ordinary acts.\n\n3. [P2, Architecture/stream lifecycle and failures] Make the new RPC update decoder preserve cancellation and the ArtroomError boundary on native byte streams. decodeUpdates at packages/client/src/room.ts:579-619 eagerly locks bytes with getReader, but cancel delegates to bytes.cancel while that lock is held. A native ReadableStream test confirms updates.cancel rejects TypeError even before the caller asks for an update reader, does not call the source's cancel handler, and leaves the source locked. Real Workers RPC streams have Streams API behavior; the fake byte streams have no lock checks and hide this defect. Also, fatal UTF-8 decoding at line 608 throws a raw TypeError, unlike the decoder's normalized JSON errors; an independent invalid-byte test confirms isArtroomError is false. Manage source ownership and decoded-reader ownership explicitly, ensure cancel terminates/releases the underlying subscription and any pending reads, and normalize byte/decode failures with the same redacted ArtroomError contract as transport calls. Test native streams before reading, while a read is pending, after release/EOF, invalid UTF-8 and a failing source. Preserve chunk splitting and multi-byte correctness.\n\nArchitecture: one prepared act and one durable completion journal are the right direction. Their completion boundary must include local consequences, and retained signed replay must use the original room-bound envelope directly. Read sessions authorize reads, not retrieval of an already recorded signed act. The RPC adapter correctly keeps bearer signing in the Room; stream cancellation must remain reliable for long-lived agents and Workers.\n\nSecurity: the bearer redactor is now registered before the first read, the CLI scrubs ordinary output, and MCP's closed input/name checks use own properties within the exception boundary. Bearer authentication before receipt replay is correctly retained. None of the findings authorizes a revoked bearer to replay or a retired key to admit a new act; the signed replay finding concerns only the exact retained request and the Room's required idempotency result. No live secret leak or deployed exploit is claimed.\n\nSimplification: keep one journal protocol whose durable states are prepared, remotely answered, locally completed, rather than separate cleanup rules per command. Keep one direct signed-envelope replay facility alongside normal connect. Use a standard stream wrapper or an equally explicit ownership model instead of a structural fake that discards stream locking semantics.\n\nNon-blocking packaging note: changing CLI exports to ./src/main.ts still leaves the advertised export absent from its npm package. The dry-run manifest contains only README.md, bin/artroom.js, dist/artroom.js and package.json. Remove the library export if this is a bin-only package, or package a real supported exported entry. The bin builds and runs successfully. Remove the obsolete renamed redemption snapshot when next updating snapshots.\n\nProduction Room end-to-end acceptance remains required at the integration stage; the submitted fake-Room package loop is valid package evidence. Full functionality remains the target, without schedule-based exclusions.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:724bcf2a725b0db9afa2439f3116e17f1635bbe2","binding":"assigned","head":"3be00804e501e4f30e8cf653b6dd1ce8de72a25e","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c25d288a0e3025b1fdc5d3f5759d64174a93cbd6\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3f934a98fa8efcc34c1695fee9b59e58568876e3\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c25d288a0e3025b1fdc5d3f5759d64174a93cbd6","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}